{"reference":"1 Chronicles 8","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":8,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Reading the Genealogies","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter belongs to a larger sequence of genealogies. These lists may function as selective maps of kinship, land, office, and restored identity rather than as exhaustive modern-style biological pedigrees. That possibility means gaps, parallel family lines, and differing names should be considered case by case.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 1:1-54","1 Chronicles 2:1-55","1 Chronicles 3:1-24","1 Chronicles 4:1-43","1 Chronicles 5:1-26","1 Chronicles 6:1-81","1 Chronicles 7:1-40","1 Chronicles 9:1-44"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_008_b1b2a65ace1f39133a83abaa"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}